    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0296" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg178"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Phelps to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 10, 1889</date>.
                        (Received October 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 16.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department already has a large
                    collection of papers in the case of Albert Bernhard.</p>
                <p>Mr. Reid has kindly forwarded a copy of one found in the archives of the Paris
                    legation, which seems to have a peculiar value. The paper in question, dated
                    August 19, 1887, is from the Liguedes Patriotes, in answer to certain inquiries
                    made by our legation in Paris concerning Bernhard’s connection with that
                    society. A copy is herewith inclosed. It seems to show clearly, in spite of his
                    many denials, that Bernhard had actually joined the Ligue “in the quality of an
                    Alsatian,” in March, 1883.</p>
                <p>I have retained a copy for our files, which are already fairly weighted with
                    Bernhard papers.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. Walter
                    Phelps.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d128-a1.xml" xpointer="d128-a1"/>
            </div>
